    <h1 class="page-title">Every city keeps a second list</h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:22px">
      <p>It isn’t on any app. It lives in the head of the weirdo you met at a dive bar last weekend, the line cook on a smoke break, and that one cousin who somehow always knows a guy who knows a place.</p>
      <p>That list is the good one. The nine-stool noodle counter where you wait on the sidewalk with a menu. The bakery that’s sold out by nine. The bar that was pouring long before anybody thought to review it.</p>
      <p>The Unlisted is that list, written down, for people who’d rather eat well than eat famous. We take our cue from Anthony Bourdain: show up hungry, order what the regulars order, talk to whoever’s behind the counter, and be a good guest.</p>
      <p>Search engines and review sites rank what’s already popular. We go the other way. A person picks and checks every place. AI does the legwork: reading what’s been written, drafting the story, and flagging anything we couldn’t confirm. Then a human decides whether it gets in.</p>
      <p><strong>Not everything gets in. That’s the point.</strong></p>
      <p>We’re open in the Bay Area, with San Diego next. Know a door we should knock on? <a href="/suggest/">Tell us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
